x"></div>Despite their simplicity, language models are increasingly functio=
ning as the foundation for almost all language technologies from question a=
nswering to summarization. But their immense capabilities and risks are not=
 well understood. Holistic Evaluation of Language Models (HELM) is a living=
 benchmark that aims to improve the transparency of language models.<ol><li=
><b>Broad coverage and recognition of incompleteness</b>. We define a taxon=
omy over the scenarios we would ideally like to evaluate, select scenarios =
and metrics to cover the space and make explicit what is missing.<div class=
=3D"text-center"><img src=3D"https://crfm.stanford.edu/helm/latest/images/t=
axonomy-scenarios.png" style=3D"width: 300px;"></div></li><li><b>Multi-metr=
ic measurement</b>. Rather than focus on isolated metrics such as accuracy,=
 we simultaneously measure multiple metrics (e.g., accuracy, robustness, ca=
libration, efficiency) for each scenario, allowing analysis of tradeoffs.<d=
iv class=3D"text-center"><img src=3D"https://crfm.stanford.edu/helm/latest/=
images/scenarios-by-metrics.png" style=3D"width: 300px;"></div></li><li><b>=
